From: ...
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as2xxxx: only probe Aeonsemi PHYs when matching

The PHY matching callbacks are called for unrelated PHYs too. Check the
cached PCS vendor ID before modifying mmds_present or doing any MDIO
accesses. Otherwise the AS21xxx callback also attempts its vendor-specific
MDIO workaround on foreign devices.

Use the same early guard and generic matching fallback as the mainline
as21xxx driver. This adapts Mihai Ordean's fix for the SDK v1.9.2 driver
to the v2.5.3 as21xxx_match_phy_device() and as22xxx_match_phy_device()
callbacks in as2xxxx.c.

Link: https://github.com/frank-w/BPI-Router-Linux/commit/4ad7eb83042935755c2505dcc74012ba9b3e6420
Link: https://git.kernel.org/linus/b4d5cd20507b252c746fa6971d82ac96f3b3e5b7
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/as2xxxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as2xxxx.c
@@ -1784,6 +1784,11 @@ static int as21xxx_match_phy_device(stru
 	int ret;
 	int cnt = 0;

+	/* Skip foreign PHYs before changing their state or accessing MDIO. */
+	if (!phy_id_compare_vendor(phydev->c45_ids.device_ids[MDIO_MMD_PCS],
+				   PHY_VENDOR_AEONSEMI))
+		return genphy_match_phy_device(phydev, phydrv);
+
 	phydev->c45_ids.mmds_present |= MDIO_DEVS_PMAPMD | MDIO_DEVS_PCS | MDIO_DEVS_AN;

 	/* Read PHY ID to handle firmware loaded or HW reset */
@@ -1898,6 +1903,11 @@ static int as22xxx_match_phy_device(stru
 	int ret;
 	int cnt = 0;

+	/* Skip foreign PHYs before changing their state or accessing MDIO. */
+	if (!phy_id_compare_vendor(phydev->c45_ids.device_ids[MDIO_MMD_PCS],
+				   PHY_VENDOR_AEONSEMI))
+		return genphy_match_phy_device(phydev, phydrv);
+
 	phydev->c45_ids.mmds_present |= MDIO_DEVS_PMAPMD | MDIO_DEVS_PCS | MDIO_DEVS_AN;

 	/* Read PHY ID to handle firmware loaded or HW reset */
